        "title": "refactor(ui): remove dead export seams",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nRecent Control UI changes left three exports that production-mode Knip sees as dead: one test-only settings reset seam and two types used only inside their defining modules. The shrink-only dead-export ratchet therefore carried avoidable new baseline debt.\n\nFollow-up to #106153. Related: #105595.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Removed the test-only settings reset export.\n- Kept test isolation through the real successful `saveSettings` path, with safe browser globals restored before teardown cleanup.\n- Made two same-module UI types private.\n- Regenerated the production dead-export baseline immediately before push.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Production behavior stays unchanged; the internal UI export surface and ratchet baseline are smaller.\n\nNo changelog entry: internal cleanup only.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdaxravawy2xcc8jcjcmap1`: 33/33 focused UI tests passed.\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs --update` followed by `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs`: exact 3,526-entry match.\n- Baseline shrank by three entries.\n- Final post-rebase autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings, 0.94 confidence.\n",
